nge:\n\"No army can stop an idea whose time has come.\" > (A sentiment famously attributed to Hugo's philosophy, which Singh lived by.)", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:43:51Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Society of ABCs — the abased", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:44:07Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Next", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:44:40Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "7. Continuing with Victory Hugo, X was his last novel, set during the French Revolution. It deals with the conflict between revolutionary ruthlessness and human mercy. In his Jail Notebook, Singh reflected on the themes of this book. He wrestled with the idea that while revolution is \"cruel,\" it is a \"necessary surgery\" to save a dying society. Hugo’s portrayal of revolutionaries who remained principled even in the face of death deeply resonated with Singh’s own \"philosophy of the bomb.” Id X", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:44:49Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Lenin", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:44:52Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Autobiography", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:45:00Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "No", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:45:01Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Wtf", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-23T04:45:04Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "No no", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {